There are some BASIC games on the demo disk:
BINGO .BA     BLKJAC.BA     BLKJAK.BA
BUNNY .BA     CALNDR.BA     CHECKR.BA
CRAPS .BA     DICE  .BA     FOOTBL.BA
FOTBAL.BA     GOLF  .BA     HELLO .BA
HOCKEY.BA     KING  .BA     LIFE2 .BA
LIFEB .BA     MONPLY.BA     POKER .BA
ROCKET.BA     ROCKT1.BA     ROULET.BA
SIGNS .BA     SNOOPY.BA     SPACWR.BA
TICTAC.BA     WAR   .BA     WAR2  .BA
WEKDAY.BA     WUMPUS.BA     YAHTZE.BA

These games can be run with an EX command:
	.EX SNOOPY

Alternatively, one can invoke BASIC:
	.BASIC
and reply to the "NEW OR OLD" prompt:
	OLD SNOOPY

Replying
	NEW myname
allows you to write a new BASIC program.  Your new program
can be saved with a SAVE command:
	SAVE
(Note that this will require you to "save your work" when
shutting down the system!)

When BASIC is invoked this way, you may wish to use the
	BYE
command to leave BASIC and return to the dot prompt.
(Control C will also work.)
